IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `poca-nouns`

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Schedule 9 (Regulated sector and supervisory authorities) -- LAYER 1.
-- Target: main.  Schedule 9 is cited by s 330(12), s 333E(1), s 339ZG(9) and s 339ZH(11): it says what a "business in the regulated sector"
-- is and who the "supervisory authorities" are.
--
-- LABELS.  The deposited text of Schedule 9 omits the paragraph numbers (it shows only the headings and "(1)", "(2)", ...).  The numbering
-- used here is the order of the headings: para 1 Business in the regulated sector, para 2 Excluded activities, para 3 Interpretation
-- (Part 1), para 4 (Part 2, supervisory authorities, which has no heading of its own in the text), para 5 (Part 3, power to amend).
-- Para 1 is confirmed by the text itself ("paragraph 1(1)" in s 333E(2) and s 339ZG(5)(e); "paragraph 1(1)(q)" in para 2(2);
-- "paragraph 1(1)(a) to (p) or (r) to (t)" in para 2(3)(f)).  Paras 2 to 5 are inferred from order (fork register F1).
--
-- SHAPE.  Each lettered activity of para 1(1) is a BOOLEAN condition on facts the business can state.  The condition is not itself an
-- answer; the answer is the aggregate `sch 9 para 1(1)`, which is JUST TRUE when a limb holds and NOTHING otherwise
-- (the list is introduced by "to the extent that" and is not closed with "only").  Para 2 (excluded activities) is a flat negative:
-- JUST FALSE when an exclusion holds, NOTHING otherwise.  The two are gathered by hand in `sch 9 paras 1 and 2` (option B of ruling E1).
-- Terms the Schedule borrows from other instruments (the Money Laundering Regulations 2017, the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000
-- and its Orders, the Capital Requirements Regulation, the Companies Act 2006 and so on) are asked as facts.

§ `Schedule 9, Part 1: regulated sector`

§§ `sch 9 para 1(1): the limbs`

-- The chapeau.  Each lettered limb below is a CONDITION (a BOOLEAN over facts the business can state); the answer is the aggregate at the end of this group.
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:3 | Business in the regulated sector
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:4 | (1) A business is in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of—
@ref sch 9 para 1(1) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:3-4)
DECLARE `Limbs of paragraph 1(1) that hold` HAS
    `limb (a)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (c)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (d)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (e)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (f)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (g)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (h)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (i)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (j)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (ja)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (k)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (l)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (m)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (n)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (o)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (p)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (q)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (r)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (s)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (t)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (u)`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (v)`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:5 | (a) the acceptance by a credit institution of deposits or other repayable funds from the public, or the granting by a credit institution of credits for its own account;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(a) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:5)
GIVEN `the business is carried on by a credit institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `grants credits for its own account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(a) the business consists of accepting deposits or granting credits as a credit institution` MEANS
        `the business is carried on by a credit institution`
    AND (`accepts deposits or other repayable funds from the public` OR `grants credits for its own account`)

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:6 | (b) the carrying on of one or more of the activities listed in points 2 to 12 , 14 and 15 of Schedule 2 to the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 by an undertaking other than—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:7 | (i) a credit institution; ...
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:8 | (ia) an undertaking whose only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement which—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:9 | (aa) falls within section 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (debtor-creditor-supplier agreements);
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:10 | (bb) provides fixed sum credit (within the meaning given in section 10(1)(b) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (running-account credit and fixed-sum credit)) in relation to the provision of services; and
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:11 | (cc) provides financial accommodation by way of deferred payment or payment by instalments over a period not exceeding 12 months; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:12 | (ii) an undertaking whose only listed activity is trading for own account in one or more of the products listed in point 7 of Schedule 2 to the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 and which does not act on behalf of a customer (that is, a third party which is not a member of the same group as the undertaking);
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(b) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:6-12)
GIVEN `carries on one or more of the activities listed in points 2 to 12, 14 and 15 of Schedule 2 to the Money Laundering Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is a credit institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement falls within section 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (debtor-creditor-supplier agreements)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides fixed sum credit in relation to the provision of services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides financial accommodation by deferred payment or payment by instalments over a period not exceeding 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its only listed activity is trading for own account in one or more of the products listed in point 7 of Schedule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it acts on behalf of a customer (a third party which is not a member of the same group as the undertaking)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(b) the business consists of listed activities carried on by an undertaking not excluded by (i), (ia) or (ii)` MEANS
        `carries on one or more of the activities listed in points 2 to 12, 14 and 15 of Schedule 2 to the Money Laundering Regulations 2017`
    AND (NOT `the undertaking is a credit institution`)
    AND (NOT (       `its only listed activity is as a creditor under an agreement`
                 AND `the agreement falls within section 12(a) of the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (debtor-creditor-supplier agreements)`
                 AND `the agreement provides fixed sum credit in relation to the provision of services`
                 AND `the agreement provides financial accommodation by deferred payment or payment by instalments over a period not exceeding 12 months`))
    AND (NOT (       `its only listed activity is trading for own account in one or more of the products listed in point 7 of Schedule 2`
                 AND (NOT `it acts on behalf of a customer (a third party which is not a member of the same group as the undertaking)`)))

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:13 | (c) the carrying on of activities by an authorised person (within the meaning of section 31 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000) who has permission under Part 4A of that Act to carry out or effect contracts of insurance, where those activities consist of carrying out or effecting contracts of long-term insurance other than a reinsurance contract;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(c) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:13)
GIVEN `an authorised person (section 31 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000) with permission under Part 4A of that Act to carry out or effect contracts of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activities consist of carrying out or effecting contracts of long-term insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is a reinsurance contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(c) the business consists of long-term insurance other than reinsurance` MEANS
        `an authorised person (section 31 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000) with permission under Part 4A of that Act to carry out or effect contracts of insurance`
    AND `the activities consist of carrying out or effecting contracts of long-term insurance`
    AND (NOT `the contract is a reinsurance contract`)

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:14 | (d) the provision of investment services or the performance of investment activities by a person (other than a person falling within one of the exclusions to the definition of “investment firm” in article 3(1) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544)) whose regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(d) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:14)
GIVEN `provides investment services or performs investment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `falls within one of the exclusions to the definition of "investment firm" in article 3(1) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(d) the business consists of investment services or activities by a person not excluded` MEANS
        `provides investment services or performs investment activities`
    AND (NOT `falls within one of the exclusions to the definition of "investment firm" in article 3(1) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001`)
    AND `regular occupation or business is the provision to other persons of an investment service or the performance of an investment activity on a professional basis`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:15 | (e) the marketing or other offering of units or shares by a collective investment undertaking;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(e) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:15)
GIVEN `markets or otherwise offers units or shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a collective investment undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(e) the business consists of the marketing or offering of units or shares by a collective investment undertaking` MEANS
    `markets or otherwise offers units or shares` AND `as a collective investment undertaking`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:16 | (f) the activities of an insurance intermediary as defined in article 33B(4) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001, in respect of contracts of long-term insurance within the meaning given by article 3(1) of, and Part II of Schedule 1 to, that Order;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(f) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:16)
GIVEN `the activities are those of an insurance intermediary as defined in article 33B(4) of the Regulated Activities Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in respect of contracts of long-term insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(f) the business consists of the activities of an insurance intermediary in respect of long-term insurance` MEANS
    `the activities are those of an insurance intermediary as defined in article 33B(4) of the Regulated Activities Order` AND `in respect of contracts of long-term insurance`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:17 | (g) the carrying on of any of the activities mentioned in paragraphs (b) to (f) by a branch located in the United Kingdom of a person referred to in those paragraphs (or of an equivalent person in any other State), wherever its head office is located;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(g) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:17)
GIVEN `carries on any of the activities mentioned in paragraphs (b) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by a branch located in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `of a person referred to in those paragraphs (or of an equivalent person in any other State)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(g) the business consists of activities in (b) to (f) carried on by a branch in the United Kingdom` MEANS
    `carries on any of the activities mentioned in paragraphs (b) to (f)` AND `by a branch located in the United Kingdom` AND `of a person referred to in those paragraphs (or of an equivalent person in any other State)`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:18 | (h) the activities of the National Savings Bank;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(h) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:18)
GIVEN `carries on the activities of the National Savings Bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(h) the business consists of the activities of the National Savings Bank` MEANS `carries on the activities of the National Savings Bank`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:19 | (i) any activity carried on for the purpose of raising money authorised to be raised under the National Loans Act 1968 under the auspices of the Director of Savings;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(i) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:19)
GIVEN `any activity carried on for the purpose of raising money authorised to be raised under the National Loans Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the auspices of the Director of Savings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(i) the business consists of an activity for raising money under the National Loans Act 1968` MEANS
    `any activity carried on for the purpose of raising money authorised to be raised under the National Loans Act 1968` AND `under the auspices of the Director of Savings`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:20 | (j) the carrying on of statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of the Companies Act 2006 (meaning of “statutory auditor” etc) by any firm or individual who is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of that Act (statutory auditors);
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(j) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:20)
GIVEN `carries on statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(j) the business consists of statutory audit work by a statutory auditor` MEANS
    `carries on statutory audit work within the meaning of section 1210 of the Companies Act 2006` AND `is a statutory auditor within the meaning of Part 42 of that Act`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:21 | (ja) the carrying on of local audit work within the meaning of Schedule 5 to the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014 (eligibility and regulation of local auditors) by any firm or individual who is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of that Act (general requirements for audit);
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(ja) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:21)
GIVEN `carries on local audit work within the meaning of Schedule 5 to the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(ja) the business consists of local audit work by a local auditor` MEANS
    `carries on local audit work within the meaning of Schedule 5 to the Local Audit and Accountability Act 2014` AND `is a local auditor within the meaning of section 4(1) of that Act`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:22 | (k) the activities of a person appointed to act as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (meaning of “act as insolvency practitioner”) or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(k) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:22)
GIVEN `is appointed to act as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(k) the business consists of the activities of an insolvency practitioner` MEANS
    `is appointed to act as an insolvency practitioner within the meaning of section 388 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or article 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:23 | (l) the provision to other persons of accountancy services by a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides such services to other persons;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(l) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:23)
GIVEN `provides accountancy services to other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides such services to other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(l) the business consists of the provision of accountancy services` MEANS
    `provides accountancy services to other persons` AND `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides such services to other persons`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:24 | (m) the provision of material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons by a firm or sole practitioner, whether provided directly or through a third party, if the firm or sole practitioner by way of business provides (as the case may be) aid, assistance or advice in connection with the tax affairs of other persons;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(m) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:24)
GIVEN `provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons (directly or through a third party)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides aid, assistance or advice in connection with the tax affairs of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(m) the business consists of material aid, assistance or advice in connection with tax affairs` MEANS
    `provides material aid, or assistance or advice, in connection with the tax affairs of other persons (directly or through a third party)` AND `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides aid, assistance or advice in connection with the tax affairs of other persons`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:25 | (n) the participation in financial or real property transactions concerning—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:26 | (i) the buying and selling of real property (or, in Scotland, heritable property) or business entities;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:27 | (ii) the managing of client money, securities or other assets;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:28 | (iii) the opening or management of bank, savings or securities accounts;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:29 | (iv) the organisation of contributions necessary for the creation, operation or management of companies; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:30 | (v) the creation, operation or management of trusts, companies or similar structures,
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:31 | by a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(n) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:25-31)
GIVEN `participates (para 1(3)) in the buying and selling of real property (or, in Scotland, heritable property) or business entities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participates in the managing of client money, securities or other assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participates in the opening or management of bank, savings or securities accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participates in the organisation of contributions necessary for the creation, operation or management of companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participates in the creation, operation or management of trusts, companies or similar structures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(n) the business consists of participation in a financial or real property transaction by a legal or notarial services provider` MEANS
        (   `participates (para 1(3)) in the buying and selling of real property (or, in Scotland, heritable property) or business entities`
         OR `participates in the managing of client money, securities or other assets`
         OR `participates in the opening or management of bank, savings or securities accounts`
         OR `participates in the organisation of contributions necessary for the creation, operation or management of companies`
         OR `participates in the creation, operation or management of trusts, companies or similar structures`)
    AND `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides legal or notarial services to other persons`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:32 | (o) the provision to other persons by way of business by a firm or sole practitioner of any of the services mentioned in sub-paragraph (4);
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(o) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:32)
GIVEN `provides a service mentioned in sub-paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a firm or sole practitioner providing it to other persons by way of business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(o) the business consists of a service mentioned in sub-paragraph (4)` MEANS
    `provides a service mentioned in sub-paragraph (4)` AND `a firm or sole practitioner providing it to other persons by way of business`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:33 | (p) the carrying on of estate agency work or letting agency work, ... by a firm or a sole practitioner who carries on, or whose employees carry on, such work;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(p) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:33)
GIVEN `carries on estate agency work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carries on letting agency work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a firm or a sole practitioner who carries on, or whose employees carry on, such work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(p) the business consists of estate agency work or letting agency work` MEANS
    (`carries on estate agency work` OR `carries on letting agency work`) AND `a firm or a sole practitioner who carries on, or whose employees carry on, such work`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:34 | (q) the trading in goods (including dealing as an auctioneer) whenever a transaction involves the making or receipt of a payment or payments in cash of at least £10,000 in total, whether the transaction is executed in a single operation or in several operations which appear to be linked, by a firm or sole trader who by way of business trades in goods;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(q) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:34)
GIVEN `trades in goods (including dealing as an auctioneer)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments in cash made or received in the transaction (or in several operations which appear to be linked), in pounds in total` IS A NUMBER
      `a firm or sole trader who by way of business trades in goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(q) the business consists of trading in goods where a transaction involves cash payments of at least 10,000 pounds in total` MEANS
        `trades in goods (including dealing as an auctioneer)`
    AND `the payments in cash made or received in the transaction (or in several operations which appear to be linked), in pounds in total` AT LEAST 10_000
    AND `a firm or sole trader who by way of business trades in goods`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:35 | (r) operating a casino under a casino operating licence (within the meaning given by section 65(2) of the Gambling Act 2005 (nature of licence)).
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(r) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:35)
GIVEN `operates a casino under a casino operating licence (section 65(2) of the Gambling Act 2005)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(r) the business consists of operating a casino under a casino operating licence` MEANS
    `operates a casino under a casino operating licence (section 65(2) of the Gambling Act 2005)`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:36 | (s) the auctioning by an auction platform of two-day spot or five-day futures, within the meanings given by Article 3 of the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation.
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(s) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:36)
GIVEN `auctions, by an auction platform, two-day spot or five-day futures within the meanings given by Article 3 of the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(s) the business consists of the auctioning by an auction platform of two-day spot or five-day futures` MEANS
    `auctions, by an auction platform, two-day spot or five-day futures within the meanings given by Article 3 of the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:37 | (t) bidding directly, on behalf of clients, in auctions of emissions allowances in accordance with the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation.
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(t) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:37)
GIVEN `bids directly, on behalf of clients, in auctions of emissions allowances in accordance with the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(t) the business consists of bidding directly on behalf of clients in auctions of emissions allowances` MEANS
    `bids directly, on behalf of clients, in auctions of emissions allowances in accordance with the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:38 | (u) the carrying on of activities by a firm or sole practitioner when it—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:39 | (i) by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art and the value of the transaction, or a series of linked transactions, amounts to £10,000 or more; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:40 | (ii) is the operator of a freeport when it, or any other firm or sole practitioner, stores works of art in the freeport and the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of linked persons, amounts to £10,000 or more;
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(u) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:38-40)
GIVEN `a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the transaction, or a series of linked transactions, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `is the operator of a freeport` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it, or any other firm or sole practitioner, stores works of art in the freeport` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of linked persons, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(u) the business consists of activities in works of art of 10,000 pounds or more, or storing works of art in a freeport` MEANS
        `a firm or sole practitioner`
    AND (   (    `by way of business trades in, or acts as an intermediary in the sale or purchase of, works of art`
             AND `the value of the transaction, or a series of linked transactions, in pounds` AT LEAST 10_000)
         OR (    `is the operator of a freeport`
             AND `it, or any other firm or sole practitioner, stores works of art in the freeport`
             AND `the value of the works of art so stored for a person, or a series of linked persons, in pounds` AT LEAST 10_000))

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:41 | (v) the carrying on of activities by a firm or individual when acting as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider.
@ref sch 9 para 1(1)(v) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:41)
GIVEN `a firm or individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1)(v) the business consists of activities as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider` MEANS
    `a firm or individual` AND `acts as a cryptoasset exchange provider or custodian wallet provider`

-- The aggregate.  "A business is in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of" the limbs.
-- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence is introduced by "to the extent that" and is not closed with "only", so a business
-- that fits no limb is not thereby said to be outside the regulated sector; para 2 (excluded activities) is what says "is not".
@ref sch 9 para 1(1) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:3-41)
GIVEN limbs IS A `Limbs of paragraph 1(1) that hold`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(1) the business is in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of a listed activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       limbs's `limb (a)` OR limbs's `limb (b)` OR limbs's `limb (c)` OR limbs's `limb (d)` OR limbs's `limb (e)`
              OR limbs's `limb (f)` OR limbs's `limb (g)` OR limbs's `limb (h)` OR limbs's `limb (i)` OR limbs's `limb (j)`
              OR limbs's `limb (ja)` OR limbs's `limb (k)` OR limbs's `limb (l)` OR limbs's `limb (m)` OR limbs's `limb (n)`
              OR limbs's `limb (o)` OR limbs's `limb (p)` OR limbs's `limb (q)` OR limbs's `limb (r)` OR limbs's `limb (s)`
              OR limbs's `limb (t)` OR limbs's `limb (u)` OR limbs's `limb (v)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "to the extent that it consists of" (no "only")

§§ `sch 9 para 1(2) to (13): definitions used by the limbs`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:42 | (2) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(a) and (b) “credit institution” means—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:43 | (a) a credit institution as defined in Article 4(1)(1) of the Capital Requirements Regulation; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:44 | (b) a branch (within the meaning of Article 4(1)(17) of that Regulation) located in the United Kingdom of an institution falling within paragraph (a) (or of an equivalent institution in any other State) wherever its head office is located.
@ref sch 9 para 1(2) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:42-44)
GIVEN `a credit institution as defined in Article 4(1)(1) of the Capital Requirements Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a branch within the meaning of Article 4(1)(17) of that Regulation located in the United Kingdom of an institution falling within paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a branch located in the United Kingdom of an equivalent institution in any other State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(2) the person is a credit institution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a credit institution as defined in Article 4(1)(1) of the Capital Requirements Regulation` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a branch within the meaning of Article 4(1)(17) of that Regulation located in the United Kingdom of an institution falling within paragraph (a)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a branch located in the United Kingdom of an equivalent institution in any other State` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“credit institution” means"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:45 | (2A) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(c), “contract of long-term insurance” means any contract falling within Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001 (S.I. 2001/544).
@ref sch 9 para 1(2A) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:45)
GIVEN `the contract falls within Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(2A) the contract is a contract of long-term insurance` MEANS
    IF `the contract falls within Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“contract of long-term insurance” means any contract falling within Part 2 of Schedule 1"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:46 | (3) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(n) a person participates in a transaction by assisting in the planning or execution of the transaction or otherwise acting for or on behalf of a client in the transaction.
@ref sch 9 para 1(3) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:46)
GIVEN `assists in the planning or execution of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `otherwise acts for or on behalf of a client in the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(3) the person participates in the transaction` MEANS
    IF `assists in the planning or execution of the transaction` OR `otherwise acts for or on behalf of a client in the transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "participates in a transaction by assisting ... or otherwise acting" does not say "only"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:47 | (4) The services referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(o) are—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:48 | (a) forming companies or other legal persons;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:49 | (ab) selling an off-the-shelf firm
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:50 | (b) acting, or arranging for another person to act—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:51 | (i) as a director or secretary of a company;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:52 | (ii) as a partner of a partnership; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:53 | (iii) in a similar position in relation to other legal persons;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:54 | (c) providing a registered office, business address, correspondence or administrative address or other related services for a company, partnership or any other legal person or arrangement;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:55 | (d) acting, or arranging for another person to act, as—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:56 | (i) a trustee of an express trust or similar legal arrangement; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:57 | (ii) a nominee shareholder for a person other than a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market.
@ref sch 9 para 1(4) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:47-57)
GIVEN `forms companies or other legal persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sells an off-the-shelf firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a director or secretary of a company, as a partner of a partnership, or in a similar position in relation to other legal persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provides a registered office, business address, correspondence or administrative address or other related services for a company, partnership or any other legal person or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a trustee of an express trust or similar legal arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a nominee shareholder for a person other than a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(4) the service is one referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(o)` MEANS
    IF       `forms companies or other legal persons`
          OR `sells an off-the-shelf firm`
          OR `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a director or secretary of a company, as a partner of a partnership, or in a similar position in relation to other legal persons`
          OR `provides a registered office, business address, correspondence or administrative address or other related services for a company, partnership or any other legal person or arrangement`
          OR `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a trustee of an express trust or similar legal arrangement`
          OR `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a nominee shareholder for a person other than a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The services referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(o) are" does not say "only"

-- The one limb of the list that the text carves out in its own words: (4)(d)(ii) is a nominee shareholder "for a person other than a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market".
-- A nominee for a listed company is therefore not within limb (d)(ii) (JUST FALSE); the list as a whole stays open (the rule above answers NOTHING when no limb applies).
@ref sch 9 para 1(4)(d)(ii) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:57)
GIVEN `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a nominee shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person for whom the nominee acts is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(4)(d)(ii) the service is acting as a nominee shareholder for a person other than a listed company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a nominee shareholder` AND (NOT `the person for whom the nominee acts is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `acts, or arranges for another person to act, as a nominee shareholder` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a nominee shareholder for a person other than a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The services referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(o) are" does not say "only", so a service that is not a nominee shareholder at all is not answered by this limb

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:58 | (4A) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4)(ab), an “off-the-shelf firm” means a firm that either—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:59 | (a) does not carry on business; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:60 | (b) carries on business but such business is not the main activity carried on by the firm or sole practitioner.
@ref sch 9 para 1(4A) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:58-60)
GIVEN `does not carry on business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carries on business but such business is not the main activity carried on by the firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(4A) the firm is an off-the-shelf firm` MEANS
    IF `does not carry on business` OR `carries on business but such business is not the main activity carried on by the firm or sole practitioner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an “off-the-shelf firm” means a firm that either"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:61 | (5) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (4)(d) “regulated market” has the meaning given by regulation 3(1) (general interpretation) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692).
@ref sch 9 para 1(5) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:61)
GIVEN `a regulated market within regulation 3(1) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(5) the market is a regulated market` MEANS
    IF `a regulated market within regulation 3(1) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given by regulation 3(1)" of the 2017 Regulations, which are not among the sources

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:63 | (6A) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(p) “estate agency work” is to be read in accordance with section 1 of the Estate Agents Act 1979 (estate agency work), but for those purposes references in that section to disposing of or acquiring an interest in land are (despite anything in section 2 of that Act) to be taken to include references to disposing of or acquiring an estate or interest in land outside the United Kingdom where that estate or interest is capable of being owned or held as a separate interest.
@ref sch 9 para 1(6A) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:63)
GIVEN `is estate agency work to be read in accordance with section 1 of the Estate Agents Act 1979` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is disposing of or acquiring an estate or interest in land outside the United Kingdom, capable of being owned or held as a separate interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(6A) the work is estate agency work` MEANS
    IF `is estate agency work to be read in accordance with section 1 of the Estate Agents Act 1979` OR `is disposing of or acquiring an estate or interest in land outside the United Kingdom, capable of being owned or held as a separate interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "is to be read in accordance with section 1 of the Estate Agents Act 1979", which is not among the sources

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:64 | (6B) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(p) “letting agency work” means work—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:65 | (a) consisting of things done in response to instructions received from—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:66 | (i) a person (a “prospective landlord”) seeking to find another person to whom to let land, or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:67 | (ii) a person (a “prospective tenant”) seeking to find land to rent, and
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:68 | (b) done in a case where an agreement is concluded for the letting of land—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:69 | (i) for a term of a month or more, and
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:70 | (ii) at a rent which during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent of £10,000 or more.
@ref sch 9 para 1(6B) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:64-70)
GIVEN `done in response to instructions from a person (a prospective landlord) seeking to find another person to whom to let land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `done in response to instructions from a person (a prospective tenant) seeking to find land to rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `done in a case where an agreement is concluded for the letting of land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letting is for a term of a month or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rent during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent in pounds of` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(6B) the work is letting agency work` MEANS
    IF       (`done in response to instructions from a person (a prospective landlord) seeking to find another person to whom to let land` OR `done in response to instructions from a person (a prospective tenant) seeking to find land to rent`)
         AND `done in a case where an agreement is concluded for the letting of land`
         AND `the letting is for a term of a month or more`
         AND `the rent during at least part of the term is, or is equivalent to, a monthly rent in pounds of` AT LEAST 10_000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“letting agency work” means work"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:71 | (6C) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(p) “letting agency work” does not include the things listed in sub-paragraph (6D) when done by, or by employees of, a firm or sole practitioner if neither the firm or sole practitioner, nor any of their employees, does anything else within sub-paragraph (6B).
@ref sch 9 para 1(6C) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:71)
GIVEN `the thing done is one listed in sub-paragraph (6D)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `done by, or by employees of, a firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `neither the firm or sole practitioner, nor any of their employees, does anything else within sub-paragraph (6B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(6C) the thing done is letting agency work` MEANS
    IF       `the thing done is one listed in sub-paragraph (6D)`
         AND `done by, or by employees of, a firm or sole practitioner`
         AND `neither the firm or sole practitioner, nor any of their employees, does anything else within sub-paragraph (6B)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“letting agency work” does not include the things listed in sub-paragraph (6D)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion applies only when the thing is done by the firm and nothing else within (6B) is done

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:72 | (6D) Those things are—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:73 | (a) publishing advertisements or disseminating information;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:74 | (b) providing a means by which a prospective landlord or a prospective tenant can, in response to an advertisement or dissemination of information, make direct contact with a prospective tenant or a prospective landlord;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:75 | (c) providing a means by which a prospective landlord and a prospective tenant can communicate directly with each other;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:76 | (d) the provision of legal or notarial services by a barrister, advocate, solicitor or other legal representative communications with whom may be the subject of a claim to professional privilege or, in Scotland, protected from disclosure in legal proceedings on grounds of confidentiality of communication.
@ref sch 9 para 1(6D) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:72-76)
GIVEN `publishing advertisements or disseminating information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `providing a means by which a prospective landlord or a prospective tenant can, in response to an advertisement or dissemination of information, make direct contact with a prospective tenant or a prospective landlord` IS A BOOLEAN
      `providing a means by which a prospective landlord and a prospective tenant can communicate directly with each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision of legal or notarial services by a barrister, advocate, solicitor or other legal representative communications with whom may be the subject of a claim to professional privilege or, in Scotland, protected from disclosure in legal proceedings on grounds of confidentiality of communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(6D) the thing is one of those listed` MEANS
    IF       `publishing advertisements or disseminating information`
          OR `providing a means by which a prospective landlord or a prospective tenant can, in response to an advertisement or dissemination of information, make direct contact with a prospective tenant or a prospective landlord`
          OR `providing a means by which a prospective landlord and a prospective tenant can communicate directly with each other`
          OR `the provision of legal or notarial services by a barrister, advocate, solicitor or other legal representative communications with whom may be the subject of a claim to professional privilege or, in Scotland, protected from disclosure in legal proceedings on grounds of confidentiality of communication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Those things are" does not say "only"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:77 | (6E) In sub-paragraph (6B) “land” includes part of a building and part of any other structure.
@ref sch 9 para 1(6E) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:77)
GIVEN `land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `part of a building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `part of any other structure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(6E) the thing is land` MEANS
    IF `land` OR `part of a building` OR `part of any other structure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“land” includes part of a building and part of any other structure"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:78 | (7) For the purposes of sub-paragraphs (1)(j) and (l) to (q) and (6C) “firm” means any entity, whether or not a legal person, that is not an individual and includes a body corporate and a partnership or other unincorporated association.
@ref sch 9 para 1(7) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:78)
GIVEN `an entity, whether or not a legal person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(7) the person is a firm` MEANS
    IF `an entity, whether or not a legal person` AND (NOT `an individual`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“firm” means any entity ... that is not an individual"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:79 | (8) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(q) “cash” means notes, coins or travellers’ cheques in any currency.
@ref sch 9 para 1(8) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:79)
GIVEN `notes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `coins` IS A BOOLEAN
      `travellers' cheques` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(8) the thing is cash` MEANS
    IF `notes` OR `coins` OR `travellers' cheques`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cash” means notes, coins or travellers’ cheques in any currency"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:80 | (9) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(s) “auction platform” means a platform on which auctions of emissions allowances are held in accordance with the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation.
@ref sch 9 para 1(9) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:80)
GIVEN `a platform on which auctions of emissions allowances are held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in accordance with the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(9) the platform is an auction platform` MEANS
    IF `a platform on which auctions of emissions allowances are held` AND `in accordance with the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“auction platform” means a platform on which auctions of emissions allowances are held"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:81 | (10) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(u), “work of art” means anything which, in accordance with section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994 (value of imported goods), is a work of art for the purposes of section 21(5)(a) of that Act.
@ref sch 9 para 1(10) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:81)
GIVEN `is a work of art in accordance with section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994, for the purposes of section 21(5)(a) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(10) the thing is a work of art` MEANS
    IF `is a work of art in accordance with section 21(6) to (6B) of the Value Added Tax Act 1994, for the purposes of section 21(5)(a) of that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the whole of the test is the Value Added Tax Act 1994 s 21(5)(a) and (6) to (6B), which are not among the sources

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:82 | (11) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(u), “freeport” means a warehouse or storage facility within an area designated by the Treasury as a special area for customs purposes pursuant to section 100A(1) of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979.
@ref sch 9 para 1(11) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:82)
GIVEN `a warehouse or storage facility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within an area designated by the Treasury as a special area for customs purposes pursuant to section 100A(1) of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(11) the place is a freeport` MEANS
    IF `a warehouse or storage facility` AND `within an area designated by the Treasury as a special area for customs purposes pursuant to section 100A(1) of the Customs and Excise Management Act 1979`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“freeport” means a warehouse or storage facility within an area designated by the Treasury"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:83 | (12) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(v)—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:84 | (a) “cryptoasset exchange provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides one or more of the following services, including where the firm or sole practitioner does so as creator or issuer of any of the cryptoassets involved—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:85 | (i) exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets,
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:86 | (ii) exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, one cryptoasset for another, or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:87 | (iii) operating a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:88 | (b) “custodian wallet provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides services to safeguard, or to safeguard and administer—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:89 | (i) cryptoassets on behalf of its customers, or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:90 | (ii) private cryptographic keys on behalf of its customers in order to hold, store and transfer cryptoassets.
@ref sch 9 para 1(12) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:83-90)
GIVEN `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, one cryptoasset for another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `operating a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `safeguarding, or safeguarding and administering, cryptoassets on behalf of its customers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `safeguarding, or safeguarding and administering, private cryptographic keys on behalf of its customers in order to hold, store and transfer cryptoassets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(12) the person is a cryptoasset exchange provider or a custodian wallet provider` MEANS
    IF       `a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides services`
         AND (   `exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets`
              OR `exchanging, or arranging or making arrangements with a view to the exchange of, one cryptoasset for another`
              OR `operating a machine which utilises automated processes to exchange cryptoassets for money or money for cryptoassets`
              OR `safeguarding, or safeguarding and administering, cryptoassets on behalf of its customers`
              OR `safeguarding, or safeguarding and administering, private cryptographic keys on behalf of its customers in order to hold, store and transfer cryptoassets`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cryptoasset exchange provider” means a firm or sole practitioner who by way of business provides one or more of the following services" and "“custodian wallet provider” means"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:91 | (13) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (12)—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:92 | (a) “cryptoasset” means a cryptographically secured digital representation of value or contractual rights that uses a form of distributed ledger technology and can be transferred, stored or traded electronically;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:93 | (b) “money” means—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:94 | (i) money in sterling,
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:95 | (ii) money in any other currency, or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:96 | (iii) money in any other medium of exchange,
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:97 | but does not include a cryptoasset; and
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:98 | (c) in sub-paragraphs (i), (ii) and (iii) of sub-paragraph (12)(a), “cryptoasset” includes a right to, or interest in, the cryptoasset.
@ref sch 9 para 1(13) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:91-98)
GIVEN `a cryptographically secured digital representation of value or contractual rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `uses a form of distributed ledger technology` IS A BOOLEAN
      `can be transferred, stored or traded electronically` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a right to, or interest in, a cryptoasset (in sub-paragraphs (12)(a)(i), (ii) and (iii))` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(13)(a) and (c) the thing is a cryptoasset` MEANS
    IF       (    `a cryptographically secured digital representation of value or contractual rights`
              AND `uses a form of distributed ledger technology`
              AND `can be transferred, stored or traded electronically`)
          OR `is a right to, or interest in, a cryptoasset (in sub-paragraphs (12)(a)(i), (ii) and (iii))`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“cryptoasset” means a cryptographically secured digital representation of value or contractual rights that uses a form of distributed ledger technology and can be transferred, stored or traded electronically"

@ref sch 9 para 1(13)(b) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:91-98)
GIVEN `money in sterling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `money in any other currency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `money in any other medium of exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cryptoasset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1(13)(b) the thing is money` MEANS
    IF (`money in sterling` OR `money in any other currency` OR `money in any other medium of exchange`) AND (NOT `a cryptoasset`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“money” means ... but does not include a cryptoasset"

§§ `sch 9 para 2: excluded activities`

-- Para 2 is a flat negative ("A business is not in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of"): JUST FALSE when an exclusion holds
-- (ruling N2), NOTHING otherwise (the sentence is silent about a business that none of the exclusions fits).
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:99 | Excluded activities
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:100 | (1) A business is not in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of—
@ref sch 9 para 2(1) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:99-100)
DECLARE `Exclusions of paragraph 2(1) that hold` HAS
    `exclusion (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusion (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusion (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusion (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusion (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusion (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exclusion (h)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:101 | (a) the issuing of withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 24 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014 (maximum interest in a society's withdrawable shares), or the acceptance of deposits from the public within the limit set by section 67(2) of that Act (registered society with withdrawable share capital not to carry on banking etc), by a registered society within the meaning of that Act;
@ref sch 9 para 2(1)(a) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:101)
GIVEN `issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 24 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014, or accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 67(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a registered society within the meaning of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1)(a) the business consists of a registered society's issuing of withdrawable share capital or acceptance of deposits within the limits` MEANS
    `issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 24 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014, or accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 67(2) of that Act` AND `a registered society within the meaning of that Act`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:102 | (b) the issuing of withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 6 of the Industrial and Provident Societies Act (Northern Ireland) 1969 (maximum shareholding in society), or the acceptance of deposits from the public within the limit set by section 7(3) of that Act (carrying on of banking by societies), by a society registered under that Act;
@ref sch 9 para 2(1)(b) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:102)
GIVEN `issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 6 of the Industrial and Provident Societies Act (Northern Ireland) 1969, or accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 7(3) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a society registered under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1)(b) the business consists of a registered Northern Ireland society's issuing of withdrawable share capital or acceptance of deposits within the limits` MEANS
    `issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 6 of the Industrial and Provident Societies Act (Northern Ireland) 1969, or accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 7(3) of that Act` AND `a society registered under that Act`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:103 | (c) the carrying on of any activity in respect of which a person who is (or falls within a class of persons) specified in any of paragraphs 2 to 23, 26 to 38 , 40 to 49 or 58 of the Schedule to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Exemption) Order 2001 is exempt;
@ref sch 9 para 2(1)(c) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:103)
GIVEN `carries on an activity in respect of which a person who is (or falls within a class of persons) specified in any of paragraphs 2 to 23, 26 to 38, 40 to 49 or 58 of the Schedule to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Exemption) Order 2001 is exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1)(c) the business consists of an activity for which a person specified in the Exemption Order is exempt` MEANS
    `carries on an activity in respect of which a person who is (or falls within a class of persons) specified in any of paragraphs 2 to 23, 26 to 38, 40 to 49 or 58 of the Schedule to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Exemption) Order 2001 is exempt`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:104 | (d) the exercise of the functions specified in section 45 of the Financial Services Act 1986 (miscellaneous exemptions) by a person who was an exempted person for the purposes of that section immediately before its repeal; ...
@ref sch 9 para 2(1)(d) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:104)
GIVEN `exercises the functions specified in section 45 of the Financial Services Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person who was an exempted person for the purposes of that section immediately before its repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1)(d) the business consists of the exercise of functions under section 45 of the Financial Services Act 1986 by a formerly exempted person` MEANS
    `exercises the functions specified in section 45 of the Financial Services Act 1986` AND `a person who was an exempted person for the purposes of that section immediately before its repeal`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:105 | (e) the engaging in financial activity which fulfils all of the conditions set out in paragraphs (a) to (g) of sub-paragraph (3) of this paragraph by a person whose main activity is that of a high value dealer; ...
@ref sch 9 para 2(1)(e) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:105)
GIVEN `engages in financial activity which fulfils all of the conditions set out in paragraphs (a) to (g) of sub-paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person whose main activity is that of a high value dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1)(e) the business consists of financial activity meeting the conditions in sub-paragraph (3) by a high value dealer` MEANS
    `engages in financial activity which fulfils all of the conditions set out in paragraphs (a) to (g) of sub-paragraph (3)` AND `a person whose main activity is that of a high value dealer`

-- (f) is shown blank in the text ("repealed or blank in this text"); see the coverage table.
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:106 | (f) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:107 | (g) the carrying on by a local authority (within the meaning given in article 3(1) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Regulated Activities) Order 2001) of an activity which would be a regulated activity for the purposes of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 but for article 72G of that Order; or
@ref sch 9 para 2(1)(g) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:106-107)
GIVEN `carries on an activity which would be a regulated activity for the purposes of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 but for article 72G of the Regulated Activities Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a local authority within the meaning given in article 3(1) of that Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1)(g) the business consists of an activity of a local authority that would be regulated but for article 72G` MEANS
    `carries on an activity which would be a regulated activity for the purposes of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 but for article 72G of the Regulated Activities Order` AND `a local authority within the meaning given in article 3(1) of that Order`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:108 | (h) the preparation of a home report, which for these purposes means the documents prescribed for the purposes of sections 98, 99(1) or 101(2) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2006.
@ref sch 9 para 2(1)(h) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:108)
GIVEN `prepares a home report, the documents prescribed for the purposes of sections 98, 99(1) or 101(2) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1)(h) the business consists of the preparation of a home report` MEANS
    `prepares a home report, the documents prescribed for the purposes of sections 98, 99(1) or 101(2) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2006`

@ref sch 9 para 2(1) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:99-108)
GIVEN exclusions IS A `Exclusions of paragraph 2(1) that hold`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(1) the business is in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of an excluded activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       exclusions's `exclusion (a)` OR exclusions's `exclusion (b)` OR exclusions's `exclusion (c)` OR exclusions's `exclusion (d)`
              OR exclusions's `exclusion (e)` OR exclusions's `exclusion (g)` OR exclusions's `exclusion (h)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A business is not in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion speaks only of a business "to the extent that it consists of" an excluded activity

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:109 | (2) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(e) a “high value dealer” means a person mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(q) when carrying on the activities mentioned in that paragraph.
@ref sch 9 para 2(2) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:109)
GIVEN `a person mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(q)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carrying on the activities mentioned in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(2) the person is a high value dealer` MEANS
    IF `a person mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(q)` AND `carrying on the activities mentioned in that paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “high value dealer” means a person mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(q) when carrying on the activities"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:110 | (3) A business is not in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of financial activity if—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:111 | (a) the person’s total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity does not exceed £100,000;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:112 | (b) the financial activity is limited in relation to any customer to no more than one transaction exceeding £1,000, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation, or a series of operations which appear to be linked;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:113 | (c) the financial activity does not exceed 5% of the person’s total annual turnover;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:114 | (d) the financial activity is ancillary to the person’s main activity and directly related to that activity;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:115 | (e) the financial activity is not the transmission or remittance of money (or any representation of monetary value) by any means;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:116 | (f) the main activity of the person carrying on the financial activity is not an activity mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) to (p) or (r) to (t); and
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:117 | (g) the financial activity is provided only to customers of the person’s main activity and is not offered to the public.
@ref sch 9 para 2(3) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:110-117)
GIVEN `the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the greatest number of transactions exceeding 1,000 pounds with any one customer (whether carried out in a single operation or a series of operations which appear to be linked)` IS A NUMBER
      `the financial activity as a percentage of the person's total annual turnover` IS A NUMBER
      `the financial activity is ancillary to the person's main activity and directly related to that activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial activity is the transmission or remittance of money (or any representation of monetary value) by any means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the main activity of the person is an activity mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) to (p) or (r) to (t)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial activity is provided only to customers of the person's main activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial activity is offered to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(3) the business is in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of financial activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       `the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity, in pounds` AT MOST 100_000
             AND `the greatest number of transactions exceeding 1,000 pounds with any one customer (whether carried out in a single operation or a series of operations which appear to be linked)` AT MOST 1
             AND `the financial activity as a percentage of the person's total annual turnover` AT MOST 5
             AND `the financial activity is ancillary to the person's main activity and directly related to that activity`
             AND (NOT `the financial activity is the transmission or remittance of money (or any representation of monetary value) by any means`)
             AND (NOT `the main activity of the person is an activity mentioned in paragraph 1(1)(a) to (p) or (r) to (t)`)
             AND `the financial activity is provided only to customers of the person's main activity`
             AND (NOT `the financial activity is offered to the public`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A business is not in the regulated sector to the extent that it consists of financial activity if"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion applies only if all of paragraphs (a) to (g) hold; otherwise the sub-paragraph is silent

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:118 | (4) A business is not in the regulated sector if it is carried on by—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:119 | (a) the Auditor General for Scotland;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:120 | (b) the Auditor General for Wales;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:121 | (c) the Bank of England (acting otherwise than in its capacity as the Prudential Regulation Authority);
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:122 | (d) the Comptroller and Auditor General;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:123 | (e) the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:124 | (f) the Official Solicitor to the Supreme Court, when acting as trustee in his official capacity; or
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:125 | (g) the Treasury Solicitor.
@ref sch 9 para 2(4) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:118-125)
GIVEN `the business is carried on by` IS A `Body whose business is not in the regulated sector`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 2(4) the business is in the regulated sector` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the business is carried on by` EQUALS `another body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A business is not in the regulated sector if it is carried on by" the seven bodies; it is silent about any other body
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A business is not in the regulated sector if it is carried on by"

DECLARE `Body whose business is not in the regulated sector` IS ONE OF
    `the Auditor General for Scotland`
    `the Auditor General for Wales`
    `the Bank of England (acting otherwise than in its capacity as the Prudential Regulation Authority)`
    `the Comptroller and Auditor General`
    `the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland`
    `the Official Solicitor to the Supreme Court, when acting as trustee in his official capacity`
    `the Treasury Solicitor`
    `another body`

§§ `sch 9 para 1 and 2 together`

-- Option B of ruling E1, by hand: the two sub-paragraphs each give a partial answer to ONE question ("is this business in the regulated sector?"),
-- so the question is answered by gathering them.  Para 2 (a flat negative) wins over para 1 (an inclusion), because para 2 says "not ... to the extent".
-- The order is this encoding's, not the Schedule's: the Schedule states no priority between para 1(1) and para 2 (fork register F4).
GIVEN `the answer under para 1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under para 2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under para 2(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under para 2(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 paras 1 and 2 the business is in the regulated sector` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer under para 2(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): sch 9 para 2(1) "is not in the regulated sector"
        IF `the answer under para 2(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): sch 9 para 2(3) "is not in the regulated sector"
        IF `the answer under para 2(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): sch 9 para 2(4) "is not in the regulated sector"
        OTHERWISE `the answer under para 1(1)`

§§ `sch 9 para 3: interpretation`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:126 | Interpretation
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:127 | (1) In this Part—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:130 | “the Capital Requirements Regulation” means Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 June 2013 on prudential requirements for credit institutions and investment firms;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:131 | “the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation” means Commission Regulation (EU) No. 1031/2010 of 12 November 2010 on the timing, administration and other aspects of auctioning of greenhouse gas emission allowances pursuant to Directive 2003/87/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council establishing a scheme for greenhouse gas emission allowances trading within the Community;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:135 | “the Markets in Financial Instruments Directive” means directive 2014/65/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 on markets in financial instruments.
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:136 | “the Solvency 2 Directive” means Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 25 November 2009 on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II);
@ref sch 9 para 3(1) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:126-136)
GIVEN term IS A `Instrument defined in paragraph 3(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`sch 9 para 3(1) what the defined instrument means` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `the Capital Requirements Regulation` THEN JUST "Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 26 June 2013 on prudential requirements for credit institutions and investment firms"
    WHEN `the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation` THEN JUST "Commission Regulation (EU) No. 1031/2010 of 12 November 2010 on the timing, administration and other aspects of auctioning of greenhouse gas emission allowances pursuant to Directive 2003/87/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council establishing a scheme for greenhouse gas emission allowances trading within the Community"
    WHEN `the Markets in Financial Instruments Directive` THEN JUST "directive 2014/65/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council of 15 May 2014 on markets in financial instruments"
    WHEN `the Solvency 2 Directive` THEN JUST "Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 25 November 2009 on the taking-up and pursuit of the business of Insurance and Reinsurance (Solvency II)"
    WHEN `another instrument` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "In this Part" defines these four terms and says nothing of any other instrument; the lines shown as "..." in the text are omitted words

DECLARE `Instrument defined in paragraph 3(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the Capital Requirements Regulation`
    `the Emission Allowance Auctioning Regulation`
    `the Markets in Financial Instruments Directive`
    `the Solvency 2 Directive`
    `another instrument`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:137 | (2) In this Part references to amounts in euros include references to equivalent amounts in another currency.
@ref sch 9 para 3(2) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:137)
GIVEN `the amount is in euros` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is the equivalent in another currency of an amount in euros` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 3(2) the amount is within a reference to an amount in euros` MEANS
    IF `the amount is in euros` OR `the amount is the equivalent in another currency of an amount in euros`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to amounts in euros include references to equivalent amounts in another currency"

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:138 | (3) Terms used in this Part and in the Capital Requirements Regulation... or the Markets in Financial Instruments Directive have the same meaning in this Part as in that Regulation or in that Directive.
@ref sch 9 para 3(3) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:138)
GIVEN `the term is used in this Part and in the Capital Requirements Regulation or the Markets in Financial Instruments Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 3(3) the term has the same meaning in this Part as in that Regulation or Directive` MEANS
    IF `the term is used in this Part and in the Capital Requirements Regulation or the Markets in Financial Instruments Directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph speaks only of "Terms used in this Part and in" the Regulation or the Directive

§ `Schedule 9, Part 2: supervisory authorities`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:139 | PART 2 — SUPERVISORY AUTHORITIES
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:140 | (1) The following bodies are supervisory authorities—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:141 | (a) the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:142 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:143 | (c) Financial Conduct Authority;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:144 | (d) the Gambling Commission;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:145 | (e) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:146 | (ea) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:147 | (f) ... and
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:148 | (g) the professional bodies listed in sub-paragraph (2).
@ref sch 9 para 4(1) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:139-148)
GIVEN body IS A `Body considered under paragraph 4`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 4(1) the body is a supervisory authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Financial Conduct Authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Gambling Commission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a professional body listed in sub-paragraph (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following bodies are supervisory authorities" does not say "only"; paragraphs (b), (e), (ea) and (f) are shown blank in the text

DECLARE `Body considered under paragraph 4` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    `the Financial Conduct Authority`
    `the Gambling Commission`
    `a professional body listed in sub-paragraph (2)`
    `another body`

-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:149 | (2) The professional bodies referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(g) are—
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:150 | (a) the Association of Accounting Technicians;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:151 | (b) the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:152 | (c) the Association of International Accountants;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:153 | (d) the Association of Taxation Technicians;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:154 | (da) the Chartered Institute of Legal Executives;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:155 | (e) the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:156 | (f) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:157 | (g) the Chartered Institute of Taxation;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:158 | (h) the Council for Licensed Conveyancers;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:159 | (i) the Faculty of Advocates;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:160 | (j) the Faculty Office of the Archbishop of Canterbury;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:161 | (k) the General Council of the Bar;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:162 | (l) the General Council of the Bar of Northern Ireland;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:163 | (m) the Insolvency Practitioners Association;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:164 | (n) the Institute of Certified Bookkeepers;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:165 | (o) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:166 | (p) the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:167 | (q) the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:168 | (r) the Institute of Financial Accountants;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:169 | (s) the International Association of Book-keepers;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:170 | (t) the Law Society;
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:171 | (u) the Law Society for Northern Ireland; and
-- src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:172 | (v) the Law Society of Scotland.
@ref sch 9 para 4(2) (src:ukpga-2002-29-schedule-9:149-172)
GIVEN body IS A `Professional body considered under paragraph 4(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 4(2) the body is a professional body referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(g)` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `another professional body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The professional bodies referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(g) are" does not say "only"; paragraph (f) is shown blank in the text
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Professional body considered under paragraph 4(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the Association of Accounting Technicians`
    `the Association of Chartered Certified Accountants`
    `the Association of International Accountants`
    `the Association of Taxation Technicians`
    `the Chartered Institute of Legal Executives`
    `the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants`
    `the Chartered Institute of Taxation`
    `the Council for Licensed Conveyancers`
    `the Faculty of Advocates`
    `the Faculty Office of the Archbishop of Canterbury`
    `the General Council of the Bar`
    `the General Council of the Bar of Northern Ireland`
    `the Insolvency Practitioners Association`
    `the Institute of Certified Bookkeepers`
    `the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales`
    `the Institute of Chartered Accountants in Ireland`
    `the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Scotland`
    `the Institute of Financial Accountants`
    `the International Association of Book-keepers`
    `the Law Society`
    `the Law Society for Northern Ireland`
    `the Law Society of Scotland`
    `another professional body`

§ `Schedule 9, Part 3: power to amend`

-- sch 9 para 5 ("The Treasury may by order amend Part 1 or 2 of this Schedule") is a power to amend this Schedule, which is machinery
-- (inert, reason 2).  Its effect on a person is that the lists above may change: an amended Schedule is a different text and a different encoding.
